From the project folder in Command Prompt, run:

  .venv\Scripts\python.exe app\server.py

  Then open http://127.0.0.1:8000/app/dashboard.html in your browser. Keep the terminal window open while using the app; press Ctrl+C to stop the server.

  If that Python command fails because the virtual environment is broken, recreate it and install dependencies:

  py -m venv .venv
  .venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
  .venv\Scripts\python.exe app\server.py

  The Kronos source must also be present under vendor\Kronos-master; if it isn’t, run setup_kronos.bat first.